<Wizard::IntroContent
  @imageAlt="Diagram of a user authenticating with an auth method, then passing MFA with TOTP, PingID, Okta, or Duo before Vault issues a token"
  @imageCaption="To access Vault, a user/app must present an authentication method and validate through MFA"
  @imageSrc={{img-path "~/mfa-intro.png"}}
>
  <:description>
    An MFA (Multi-factor authentication) enforcement adds a verification step to Vault logins. After a user authenticates,
    Vault holds the request until they confirm a TOTP passcode or approve a push notification, then issues the token.
  </:description>
  <:features>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="grid">
      <strong>Four methods.</strong>
      TOTP is built into Vault, which generates the key and QR code. Okta, Duo, and PingID send a push to the user's enrolled
      device.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="queue">
      <strong>Target an enforcement precisely.</strong>
      One enforcement can apply to an entity, a group, a specific auth mount, or every mount of an auth method type. The
      token auth method cannot use login MFA.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="shopping-cart">
      <strong>Rate limiting is not automatic.</strong>
      Vault allows five consecutive failed TOTP attempts by default. Apply per-client rate limits to your login and
      "sys/mfa/validate" paths for anything stronger.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
  </:features>
</Wizard::IntroContent>